  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Democracy Commission Small Grants Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Democracy Commission Small Grants Program: The U.S. Embassys Democracy Commission gives small grants primarily to organizations engaged in building the social and intellectual foundations of democracy, supporting an independent media, the democratic resolution of problems, and the institutionalization of open, pluralistic political processes. Small grants are to be given for promotion of civil society; free flow of information (including support for independent media); transparency and accountability in government; public education, public advocacy campaigns that promote democratic practices and principles; association building; rule of law and legal reform; Euro-Atlantic integration; youth activism; conflict resolution; human rights; environment; market economy; anti-trafficking; anti-corruption awareness campaigns and training; ethnic and minority equality; and non-partisan election activities, such as get-out-the vote campaigns and monitoring. During FY 2014, Post introduced a new category of Continuation fund to support project proposals that have potential to build from previously successful projects with added elements that significantly contribute to more open and competitive political and economic systems and the protection of human rights.</narrative>
  </description>
